# Chapter 16 Activity. Start InventoryService, then the app:
#   dotnet run --project InventoryService
#   dotnet run --project AdventureWorks
# (two terminals, both from this folder; in Visual Studio, set
# both as startup projects). Each "Expect" line is the status
# you should see. Send them in order. The order the file places
# is cancelled and then deleted, so it can run again.
@host = https://localhost:7001

###
# Live: the process answers; no checks run. Expect 200 with
# "Healthy"
GET {{host}}/health/live

###
# Ready: the database and the warehouse both answer.
# Expect 200 with "Healthy"
GET {{host}}/health/ready

###
# No X-Correlation-ID: the response carries the request's
# trace ID instead. Expect 200, and it has an X-Correlation-ID
# header
GET {{host}}/api/catalog

###
# A usable ID comes back unchanged. Expect 200, and it carries
# X-Correlation-ID: order-lab-1
GET {{host}}/api/catalog
X-Correlation-ID: order-lab-1

###
# A space makes the value unusable: replaced by the trace ID.
# Expect 200, and it has an X-Correlation-ID header
GET {{host}}/api/catalog
X-Correlation-ID: bad value

###
# Slow the warehouse down: 1.5 seconds for every call, its
# /health too. Expect 204
POST http://127.0.0.1:42132/control/delay/1500

###
# Ready gives up after one second: Degraded, which this app
# maps to 503. Expect 503
GET {{host}}/health/ready

###
# Live runs no checks, so it still answers. Expect 200
GET {{host}}/health/live

###
# Back to normal. Expect 204
POST http://127.0.0.1:42132/control/reset

###
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/health/ready

###
# An order, so orders.created and the duration have data.
# Expect 200
POST {{host}}/dev/sign-in/casey

###
# Expect 200
# @name token
GET {{host}}/api/csrf

###
# Expect 201
# @name created
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.$.token}}

{ "items": [ { "productId": 2, "quantity": 1 } ] }

###
# Cancel it. Expect 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/orders/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{token.response.body.$.token}}

###
# The Admin removes it, so the file can run again. Expect 200
POST {{host}}/dev/sign-in/avery

###
# Expect 200
# @name averyToken
GET {{host}}/api/csrf

###
# Expect 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/admin/orders/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{averyToken.response.body.$.token}}

###
# Expect 204
POST {{host}}/dev/sign-out
